 class=\"subtitle\">2026-05-09 • Daily Update</div>\n        </header>\n\n        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n            <!-- New Products Section -->\n            <section class=\"new-products\">\n                <h2>New Products <span class=\"section-count\">(5)</span></h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/bna-code\" target=\"_blank\">BNA Code</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        CLI-based AI agent that builds full-stack mobile applications directly from the terminal with a single prompt. Creates production-ready iOS and Android apps with backend, authentication, and native features pre-configured using Expo React Native.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-09</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">\"CLI agent that builds full-stack mobile apps from terminal\"</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/kodhau-senior-context-for-ai-agents\" target=\"_blank\">KodHau</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        MCP tool that provides AI agents with tribal knowledge of your team including PR history, design decisions, and review comments. Helps prevent AI from breaking production by giving it access to undocumented senior engineer knowledge.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-08</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Stop your AI from breaking prod - give it your team decisions\"</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com\" target=\"_blank\">Tracea</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Datadog for AI agents with traces, root cause analysis (RCA), and team memory capabilities. Provides observability and monitoring for AI agent workflows.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow orchestration</span>\n                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-09</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Datadog for AI agents with traces, RCA, and team memory\"</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/radiq\" target=\"_blank\">Radiq</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Product intelligence platform for the autonomous coding era. Automates the customer-to-code loop by surfacing decisions, prioritizing by evidence, generating developer-ready specs grounded in code, and pushing them to development teams.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-09</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Product intelligence for the autonomous coding era\"</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/bitfield\" target=\"_blank\">Bitfield</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Infrastructure tool for AI agents that prevents spaghetti code and enables agents to read state in under 1 nanosecond, addressing code maintainability and latency issues in AI development.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow orchestration</span>\n                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-09</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">\"No AI spaghetti code. Agents read state in under 1ns\"</div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n                <h2>Whitelist Updates <span class=\"section-count\">(10)</span></h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://claudefa.st/blog/guide/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code v2.1.128</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Latest Claude Code release with random session colors, MCP tool counts, plugin zip support, console channels for API key auth, model picker cleanup, OTEL isolation improvements, and numerous bug fixes.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-08</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">\"I use Claude Code for work every day. Honestly, after seeing the v2.1.128 update yesterday, I got chills.\"</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new/2026-w19\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code Week 19 Updates</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Load plugins from .zip archives and URLs, expanded plugin directory support, global command history search across projects using Ctrl+R, and Git worktree support with branch creation from local repositories.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-04</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor: PR Review & Parallel Build</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        New PR review experience with inline review threads, commits tab, and changes tab. Build in parallel from plans using async subagents. Split changes into PRs with quick action.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-06</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Reports of teams reducing code review time from 45 minutes to 10 minutes\"</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor: Enterprise Controls</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Enterprise admins get model access controls with granular allow/blocklists, soft spend limits with intelligent alerts, updated usage analytics tab filtering, and team marketplace updates.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-06</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor Security Review Beta</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Cursor Security Review now in beta on Teams and Enterprise plans with Security Reviewer (checks PRs for vulnerabilities) and Vulnerability Scanner (scheduled scans of codebase).\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type announcement\">announcement</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-06</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/paul-gauthier/aider/releases\" target=\"_blank\">Aider v0.56.0</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Enables prompt caching for Sonnet via OpenRouter, 8k output tokens for Sonnet via VertexAI and DeepSeek V2.5, new /report command for GitHub Issues, --chat-language switch, and bug fixes.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">\"GitHub issue about Windows installation difficulties with Aider v0.56.0\"</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot May 2026</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Copilot code review comment types now in usage metrics API. Rubber Duck in GitHub Copilot CLI now supports more models. Enterprise-managed plugins in GitHub Copilot CLI are now in public preview.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-08</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot Model Deprecations</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Upcoming deprecation of Grok Code Fast 1, GPT-4.1, and Claude Sonnet 4. Deprecation notice for GPT-5.2 and GPT-5.2-Codex.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type announcement\">announcement</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-08</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://continue.dev/docs/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Continue: Shareable Agents</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        You can now generate publicly shareable links to your agents so that others can try out your workflows. Continue's pull request inbox helps you ship code faster and with higher quality.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-01-09</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://claudefa.st/blog/guide/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code v2.1.126</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Added project purge command, broader skip-permissions, pasteable OAuth codes, skill activation telemetry, gateway model picker, Windows PowerShell detection, and security fixes.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-01</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n                <h2>Technical Insights <span class=\"section-count\">(5)</span></h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/5/y-combinator-openai-stake/\" target=\"_blank\">YC's 0.6% stake in OpenAI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        John Gruber reports that Y Combinator owns about 0.6 percent of OpenAI. At OpenAI's current $852 billion valuation, that's worth over $5 billion.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">openai</span> •\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">y-combinator</span> •\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">valuation</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"author\">John Gruber (via Simon Willison)</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/4/granite-svg-pelican/\" target=\"_blank\">Granite 4.1 LLMs Tested</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        IBM released Granite 4.1 family of LLMs (3B, 8B, 30B sizes) under Apache 2.0 license. Simon tested SVG generation capabilities across 21 different quantized variants and found results underwhelming.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">llm-release</span> •\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ibm</span> •\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">model-evaluation</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/3/claude-sycophancy/\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Sycophancy Study</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Anthropic's automatic classifier judged sycophancy by willingness to push back, maintain positions, give proportional praise, and speak frankly. Most conversations showed no sycophancy (9%), but spirituality (38%) and relationships (25%) were exceptions.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">anthropic</span> •\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">claude</span> •\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"author\">Anthropic (via Simon Willison)</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/2/sightings-feature/\" target=\"_blank\">Building with Claude Code</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon built a new 'Sightings' feature for his blog on his phone using Claude Code for web. The feature displays wildlife photos from iNaturalist with search, filters, and RSS.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">claude-code</span> •\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-assisted-programming</span> •\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">web-development</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://softwareengineeringdaily.com/2026/05/05/smartbear-and-multi-agent-qa/\" target=\"_blank\">Multi-Agent QA Podcast</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Discussion on how AI coding tools have dramatically accelerated development pace and shifted bottlenecks in the software development lifecycle. Covers multi-agent QA systems and the evolving landscape of AI-assisted quality assurance.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-coding</span> •\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">multi-agent-systems</span> •\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">qa-automation</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"author\">Software Engineering Daily</div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </main>\n\n        <footer>\n            <p>Generated by <a href=\"#\">Agent Code Daily</a> • Powered by <a href=\"#\">Claude Agent SDK</a></p>\n            <p style=\"margin-top: 5px;\">Report generated: 2026-05-09</p>\n        </footer>\n    </div>\n</body>\n</html>"
